# Line endings — normalise in the INDEX, leave the working tree to the platform.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `core.autocrlf=true` is set locally, and today every
# committed blob is LF (`git ls-files --eol` reports `i/lf` across the tree).
# But autocrlf is a *per-clone config*, not a property of the repository: a
# collaborator, a CI runner, or this same machine after a fresh clone with a
# different setting can commit CRLF blobs, and the next diff comes back full of
# phantom line-ending changes that bury the real one.
#
# `text=auto` moves that guarantee from a machine's config into the repo, where
# it belongs. Checkout still respects the platform, so Windows working files
# stay CRLF and nothing about the local workflow changes.
#
# THIS ALSO MATTERS FOR REVIEW ON THIS PROJECT SPECIFICALLY. `git status`,
# `git diff --numstat`, `grep -c $'\r'` and `cat -A` have all misreported
# working-tree line-ending damage here, because MSYS translates on read and
# autocrlf normalises on staging. That near-miss is recorded in the Ticket 3
# handoff. Verify line endings by byte count, never by git.
* text=auto

# Binary — never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary

# Generated — collapse in diffs and mark as such in language stats.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
